      "ambiguity": "The empty list is the honest answer for a first read, for a pass in which nothing moved, for a graph read that answered nothing and for the first pass after reset(). It therefore cannot be the *only* answer: a reader is told which nodes moved only by a list that is non-empty, and a repair that always answers the empty list is contradicted by the two passes that named them.",
      "purpose": "The map turns a stateless full-graph read into a per-pass delta. `serializeCheck` reads the graph once and `diffEpochs` compares it with the same instance's previous pass, so the record can say which nodes actually moved in this pass rather than which nodes exist; a WeakMap so a destroyed component is not retained, and keyed by the instance so two components checked in one frame keep their own epochs apart.",
      "answersTheOpenQuestion": "The key is the profiler instance and nothing else, so a primitive node identity cannot throw here: node ids are values inside the inner Map, and a pass whose nodes carry numeric ids records them as such (see numericNodeIds). The two-per-page error was therefore two frames, not two node identities."
    }
